WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.960
These days, it can be tough keeping track&nbsp;
of everything that's going on in the MCU.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.440
But maybe that's not such a bad thing&nbsp;
— after all, it just means more to look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.600
forward to. Here are the most exciting&nbsp;
Marvel projects coming over the horizon.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.840
WandaVision is among the more intriguing of&nbsp;
Marvel's Disney+ series. Overseen by Captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:25.280
Marvel and Black Widow screenwriter Jac Schaeffer,&nbsp;
the show features the reunion of — you guessed it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.880
— Wanda Maximoff and Vision. Of course, everyone's&nbsp;
favorite robot boyfriend was looking just a tad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:36.400
bit dead the last time he appeared, which begs&nbsp;
the question: just how is he making his return?

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.000
Well, it seems almost certain at this&nbsp;
point that WandaVision takes place at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.640
least partly within an alternate reality,&nbsp;
especially given that the series will tie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:49.360
into the events of Doctor Strange in the&nbsp;
Multiverse of Madness. The first trailer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:54.400
for WandaVision seems to confirm that the show&nbsp;
will venture to a number of different realities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:59.040
each set in a different decade and based&nbsp;
around a different style of American sitcom.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.480
The series will also bring back&nbsp;
Kat Dennings as Darcy Lewis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:07.120
as well as Randall Park as Jimmy Woo.&nbsp;
MCU newcomer Kathryn Hahn is taking on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.920
the role of Wanda and Vision's nosy neighbor&nbsp;
Agnes, while Teyonah Parris will be playing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:16.320
a grown-up version of Monica Rambeau , who&nbsp;
was last seen as a child in Captain Marvel.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.520
Thankfully, It won't be a terribly long wait to&nbsp;
discover how all of these seemingly disparate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.320
characters will come together — WandaVision&nbsp;
was originally slated to debut on Disney+&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:31.200
sometime in the spring of next year, but the&nbsp;
release date has been moved up to January 15th.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:36.880
The so-called Sony Universe of Marvel&nbsp;
Characters was born of Sony Pictures'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:42.960
deal with Marvel Studios, which allowed Marvel to&nbsp;
integrate Spider-Man into the MCU. In exchange,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:48.000
Sony continues to produce the webhead's&nbsp;
MCU-set solo outings, and also has free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.880
rein to develop its own universe based&nbsp;
on ancillary Spider-Man characters.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:58.640
This universe's inaugural effort, 2018's Venom,&nbsp;
cleaned up at the box office, while satisfying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.720
fans of the character left cold by the last&nbsp;
time the character appeared in a feature film.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:08.640
"Do you remember? Do you&nbsp;
remember what you did to me?"

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:14.560
After Venom's unexpected success, Sony was&nbsp;
quick to fast-track another Spidey-related&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:20.080
property — one that has been gestating since&nbsp;
2017. This would be Morbius, based on the "living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:25.840
vampire" and frequent Spider-Man nemesis who first&nbsp;
appeared in the pages of Marvel comics in 1971.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:31.360
The flick will star Jared Leto as Dr. Michael&nbsp;
Morbius, a brilliant biochemist whose attempts to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:37.200
cure his own potentially fatal blood disease with&nbsp;
an experimental treatment go predictably awry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:42.640
transforming him into a superpowered vampire.&nbsp;
Daniel Espinosa directs from a script by Lost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.840
in Space co-creators Matt Sazama and Burk&nbsp;
Sharpless. Of course, whether Morbius can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:53.600
match Venom's runaway success has yet to be seen&nbsp;
— but we'll know for sure on March 19th, 2021.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.040
Marvel has been promising a standalone&nbsp;
movie for Natasha Romanoff for years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:05.680
and now, on May 7th 2021, it's finally happening —&nbsp;
with Black Widow, in which Scarlett Johansson will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:10.160
reprise the role of the superspy Avenger&nbsp;
for what will likely be the last time.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:15.440
The prequel is set in the period between Captain&nbsp;
America: Civil War and Avengers: Infinity War,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:20.800
but will likely also flash back to the time before&nbsp;
Romanoff's recruitment by S.H.I.E.L.D. According&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:26.240
to director Cate Shortland, the movie will&nbsp;
find Romanoff in a dark place. Shortland says:

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.720
"In this film we get to understand her past&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:32.400
and put the pieces of herself&nbsp;
together and come out a whole person."

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:37.440
Much of the action will take place overseas, and&nbsp;
yes, it seems fans will finally get to find out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:42.240
just what went down in Budapest. Johansson's&nbsp;
co-stars include Florence Pugh and Rachel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:46.720
Weisz , who will appear as operatives who have&nbsp;
undergone the same Red Room training that honed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:52.160
Romanoff's deadly skills. Also starring is David&nbsp;
Harbour, who will portray Alexei Shostakov ,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:57.280
a.k.a. the Red Guardian, Russia's answer to&nbsp;
Captain America. Rounding out the cast will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:03.120
O-T Fagbenle as Marcus, an underworld "fixer," and&nbsp;
Ray Winstone, whose role is currently undisclosed.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:08.160
The debut for the MCU's first&nbsp;
Asian hero Shang-Chi was teased&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:12.880
in late 2018 — but until the full&nbsp;
title was revealed in July 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:18.080
the particularly exciting involvement of the&nbsp;
movie's iconic villain had only been rumored.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:24.800
Yes, on July 9th 2021, Shang-Chi and the Legend&nbsp;
of the Ten Rings will see the Master of Kung Fu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:29.520
face off against the Mandarin — the classic&nbsp;
Iron Man villain who notoriously didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:35.040
feature in Iron Man 3. As the title suggests,&nbsp;
the Ten Rings, the terrorist organization who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:39.920
kidnapped Tony Stark in Iron Man, will also&nbsp;
figure prominently into the on-screen origin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:44.640
of Shang-Chi — who is arguably the finest&nbsp;
unarmed combatant in the Marvel universe.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:49.600
Destin Daniel Cretton has been tapped to&nbsp;
direct, with Chinese-Canadian actor Simu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:55.200
Liu holding down the title role. Also confirmed to&nbsp;
be starring are Awkwafina in an undisclosed role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:59.520
as well as the legendary Chinese actor&nbsp;
Tony Leung as the Mandarin himself.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:05.360
Another long-rumored project to finally&nbsp;
be confirmed at Comic-Con in 2019 was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:09.520
the Disney+ series The Falcon and the&nbsp;
Winter Soldier, which will see Anthony&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:14.160
Mackie and Sebastian Stan reprising their&nbsp;
roles of Steve Rogers' two best buddies.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:18.400
It seems that Sam Wilson may have a bit of&nbsp;
reconciling to do between his old heroic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:23.520
identity and the new identity bequeathed to him&nbsp;
by Rogers himself at the conclusion of Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:29.040
Endgame. Exact plot details have so far been kept&nbsp;
under wraps, but we do know one thing for sure:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:34.000
the six-episode series will see the return&nbsp;
of Zemo, the man who goaded the Avengers into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:39.120
the titular conflict of Captain America: Civil&nbsp;
War, and he'll even be sporting his distinctive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:44.640
purple mask from the comics. The Handmaid's Tale&nbsp;
director Kari Skogland will helm every episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:50.720
with writing duties being handled by Empire's&nbsp;
Malcolm Spellman and John Wick's Derek Kolstad .

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:54.720
Here's a project that should ring all&nbsp;
kinds of nostalgia bells for longtime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:59.120
Marvel Comics readers. What If? is an&nbsp;
alternate universe anthology series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:04.320
which has run in various formats since&nbsp;
1977, exploring how events may have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:09.120
unfolded if crucial moments in the mainstream&nbsp;
Marvel timeline had played out differently.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:13.600
It allows readers to consider scenarios&nbsp;
both intriguing and unthinkable, and what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:18.800
it did for the comics, the Disney+ animated&nbsp;
series What If? intends to do for the MCU.

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:22.640
Like its comic-book counterpart, What&nbsp;
If? will have an anthology format,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:28.240
with each episode tackling one specific moment&nbsp;
in the MCU timeline. Disney's "Expanding the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:33.200
Universe" featurette on Disney+ confirmed the&nbsp;
premise of several of the series' episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:36.560
including "What if Peggy Carter had&nbsp;
taken the super soldier serum?",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:40.800
"What if T'Challa was Star Lord?", and&nbsp;
"What if Captain America was a zombie?"

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:45.840
The Marvel Studios Comic-Con panel revealed&nbsp;
an impressive line-up of MCU talent set to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:50.160
lend their voices, with many of the films'&nbsp;
biggest stars set to reprise their roles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:54.640
They will be joined by Jeffrey Wright in the&nbsp;
central role of Uatu the Watcher, whose job is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:59.680
to watch over the multiverse, and who will act&nbsp;
as a sort of host, tying each episode together.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:04.640
At the panel, Wright teased the practically&nbsp;
limitless possibilities the series might offer.

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:07.440
"We'll see where we take it.&nbsp;
We can take it anywhere."

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:12.000
Given the fact that it kicked off a&nbsp;
universe of Spider-Man characters which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:17.520
probably won't actually feature Spider-Man, the&nbsp;
success of Sony's Venom was a bit of a shock.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:21.920
Anchored by Tom Hardy's completely bonkers&nbsp;
performance, the film cleaned up at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:29.200
worldwide box office to the tune of $855 million&nbsp;
dollars, making a sequel pretty much obligatory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:34.560
Of course, having learned a few tricks from Marvel&nbsp;
Studios, Sony made sure to go ahead and set one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:40.320
up in advance, with a post-credits scene featuring&nbsp;
Woody Harrelson as Cletus Kasady, the psychopathic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:45.600
serial killer who will go on to become Carnage,&nbsp;
the Venom symbiote's terrifying offspring.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:50.560
One stumbling block the sequel faced was the&nbsp;
departure of Venom director Ruben Fleischer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:55.760
who had his hands full with the long-awaited&nbsp;
follow-up to his 2009 classic Zombieland. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:00.720
motion capture legend Andy Serkis has stepped up&nbsp;
to the helm, with original scribe Kelly Marcel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:05.760
already drafting a screenplay, and Hardy set&nbsp;
to return along with co-star Michelle Williams.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:08.800
Plot details are sketchy right&nbsp;
now, but one thing is certain:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.560
just as Kasady promised in that&nbsp;
stinger, there's gonna be, well…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:17.680
Carnage. Indeed, Variety confirmed&nbsp;
what everyone expected in January 2019:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:22.960
that Harrelson's homicidal symbiote will be the&nbsp;
movie's main villain. Venom: Let There Be Carnage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:28.720
was expected to hit theaters on October 2nd, 2020,&nbsp;
but was later moved to a summer 2021 release.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:35.040
Among the first batch of Marvel Disney+ series&nbsp;
is Loki, which sees Tom Hiddleston returning to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:40.000
portray the beloved trickster once more. While&nbsp;
our version of the character met a grim end in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:45.120
the brutal opening sequence of Avengers: Infinity&nbsp;
War, the series will follow the 2012 version of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:49.840
Loki who disappeared with the Tesseract during&nbsp;
the bungled time heist in Avengers: Endgame.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:54.560
According to The Hollywood Reporter, the series&nbsp;
will follow Loki as he "pops up throughout human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:59.840
history as an unlikely influencer on historical&nbsp;
events." The project has scored a showrunner who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:04.400
should know his way around this kind of material,&nbsp;
too: Michael Waldron , who has worked as a writer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:08.880
on Adult Swim's Rick and Morty and will be&nbsp;
credited as creator and executive producer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:13.280
in addition to writing the pilot.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, Kate Herron mwill direct.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:16.480
Joining Hiddleston will be&nbsp;
fellow cast members Owen Wilson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:23.040
Sophia Di Martino , Gugu Mbatha-Raw, and Richard&nbsp;
E. Grant — all in undisclosed roles. That said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:26.640
Wilson is taking on the role&nbsp;
of a man called Mr. Mobius,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:31.120
while Richard E. Grant is thought to be playing&nbsp;
an older, alternate version of Loki himself.

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:36.000
Rounding out the first round of&nbsp;
Disney+ limited series will be Hawkeye,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:40.960
which will see Jeremy Renner reprise his&nbsp;
role as the legendary wisecracking archer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:45.520
During 2019's San Diego Comic-Con,&nbsp;
Marvel debuted the series' logo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:50.000
as well as the confirmation of a long-standing&nbsp;
rumor: that the series will see the debut of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:54.720
Kate Bishop, the young protege who eventually&nbsp;
takes up the mantle of Hawkeye in the comics.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:59.360
The series is confirmed to take place after the&nbsp;
events of Avengers: Endgame, so it'll likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:04.000
see Clint Barton adjusting to a world in which&nbsp;
his beloved family has returned from the Snap,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:08.960
and his trusted ally Natasha Romanoff is no&nbsp;
more. While no plot details were announced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:13.120
Renner did share one little tidbit with&nbsp;
the Comic-Con crowd, which suggests that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:17.840
Barton's mentorship of Bishop will be key&nbsp;
to the series' narrative. Renner joked:

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:21.600
"I get to teach someone else how to&nbsp;
be a superhero without superpowers."

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:25.760
"What I get to do in the show&nbsp;
ultimately is shepherd an amazing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:29.600
character to be ultimately&nbsp;
probably a better version of me."

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:34.720
Fans have been clamoring for Kate Bishop's story&nbsp;
to make its way to the screen for some time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:37.840
but they'll have to wait a bit&nbsp;
longer to see it come to fruition:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:41.760
Hawkeye is scheduled to debut&nbsp;
on Disney+ in the fall of 2021.

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:47.360
In 2019, Marvel Studios opened&nbsp;
their Comic-Con panel with Eternals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:52.240
an interesting if lesser-known property which&nbsp;
should help anchor the cosmic side of the MCU.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:56.960
The titular race of superpowered beings&nbsp;
were created eons ago by the Celestials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:00.560
in order to defend the Earth from&nbsp;
their polar opposites, the Deviants.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:03.520
The Eternals were the brainchild&nbsp;
of the great Jack Kirby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:08.080
who created the comic in the mid-'70s&nbsp;
after his run on New Gods at DC.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:13.280
Marvel head honcho Kevin Feige has teased that&nbsp;
Eternals’ story may span "tens of thousands of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:18.320
years," telling an epic story of the kind we&nbsp;
haven't yet seen in the MCU. And the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:23.680
which will be directed by The Rider's Chloe&nbsp;
Zhao, has assembled a suitably epic cast.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:28.400
Eternals will star Richard Madden as Ikaris ,&nbsp;
a first-generation Eternal and leader of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:34.080
movie's team of heroes. Alongside him will be&nbsp;
Angelina Jolie as Thena, Gemma Chan as Sersi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:37.440
and Barry Keoghan as the&nbsp;
villainous Eternal, Druig.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:42.960
Meanwhile, Kumail Nanjiani will appear as&nbsp;
Kingo, a samurai and Bollywood movie star,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:48.480
Lauren Ridloff will play a gender-swapped version&nbsp;
of Makkari , a tinkerer and engineer, and Brian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:53.600
Tyree Henry is Phastos , a master weapons&nbsp;
maker who nevertheless prefers not to fight.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:57.600
Salma Hayek will play Ajak , another&nbsp;
gender-swapper character, while Lia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.600 --> 00:12:01.920
McHugh features as the trickster Sprite.&nbsp;
It's a heck of a cast, and although the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:06.400
Eternals may not be A-list Marvel characters,&nbsp;
there's a good chance this will become one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:11.520
the studio's biggest properties. Eternals&nbsp;
is due for release on February 12th, 2021.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:18.000
For just over a month during the summer of&nbsp;
2019, Spider-Man fans were left broken-hearted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:21.600
at the news that talks between Disney&nbsp;
and Sony Pictures had broken down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:25.600
and their shared custody agreement&nbsp;
over Spider-Man had come to an end.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:31.280
But then, in late September, the news broke that&nbsp;
the two studios had finally decided to play nice.

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:35.120
A new deal was struck which will allow&nbsp;
Marvel Studios to co-produce at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:39.200
one more Spider-Man film, and also&nbsp;
feature the character in an additional,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:44.640
as-yet undisclosed Marvel Studios picture. It's&nbsp;
been speculated that Marvel's third Spider-Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:49.440
movie will essentially be used to write the&nbsp;
wall-crawler out of the MCU in preparation for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:55.280
a move to Sony's own Spider-Verse, but the reality&nbsp;
could be a lot more complex... and a lot weirder.

00:12:55.280 --> 00:13:01.680
When J.K. Simmons reprised his role as J. Jonah&nbsp;
Jameson from Sam Raimi's Spider-Man trilogy in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:07.440
end credits of Spider-Man: Far From Home, everyone&nbsp;
suspected something strange was afoot in the MCU.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:13.360
Now, things are set to get even odder, as Marvel&nbsp;
revealed in October 2020 that Spider-Man 3 would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:18.480
pull in yet another character from a previous&nbsp;
unrelated Spider-film — with the announcement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:24.560
that Jamie Foxx would be returning as Electro,&nbsp;
his character from The Amazing Spider-Man 2.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:29.760
Since then, the return of many classic villains&nbsp;
and alternate Spider-Men have been confirmed.

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:35.040
While Far From Home teased at a multiverse that&nbsp;
ultimately turned out to be a ruse perpetuated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:40.800
by Mysterio, Simmons' and now Foxx's inclusion&nbsp;
seem to suggest the real deal is on the way:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:45.680
a fully-fledged multiverse that brings together&nbsp;
all of the past iterations of Spider-Man.

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:49.200
We'll learn more about how Marvel's&nbsp;
various Spider-Verses fit together when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:53.120
Spider-Man 3 hits theaters on December 17th, 2021.

00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:59.040
Given the fantastic character arc that&nbsp;
unravelled over his last several appearances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:01.600
speculation had been running high for some time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:05.360
that Thor would be the first Avenger&nbsp;
to land himself a fourth solo film.

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:12.640
"Because that's what -"&nbsp;
"Because that's what heroes do."

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:17.600
In July 2019, Marvel finally&nbsp;
confirmed this was the case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:23.040
with Thor: Ragnarok's Taika Waititi returning&nbsp;
to direct. But that wasn't all Marvel announced.

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:28.880
Hitting theatres on February 11th 2022, Thor:&nbsp;
Love and Thunder will see the return of Natalie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:33.600
Portman's Jane Foster, who will follow in her&nbsp;
character's recent comic book footsteps by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:39.440
picking up Mjolnir to become Thor herself. Tessa&nbsp;
Thompson will also return as Valkyrie , and Kevin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:44.880
Feige has confirmed that this time around, it will&nbsp;
be made explicit that the character is bisexual,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:49.360
a first for a major character in an MCU&nbsp;
film. It has also been all-but-confirmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:52.640
that the Guardians of the Galaxy will&nbsp;
be making an appearance in the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:57.280
and that the main villain will be played by none&nbsp;
other than Dark Knight alumnus Christian Bale.

00:14:57.280 --> 00:15:02.080
With all that in mind, it's hard not to believe&nbsp;
that Marvel will be expecting Love and Thunder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:07.520
to be one of their biggest and most popular Phase&nbsp;
4 releases. Frankly, who could argue otherwise?

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:13.760
The sequel to 2016's Doctor Strange has been&nbsp;
in development since before that flick even hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:19.120
theaters, and last year Marvel announced some new&nbsp;
details about the project. Namely, that it would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:23.440
be titled Doctor Strange in the Multiverse&nbsp;
of Madness, that it would co-star Elizabeth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:28.720
Olsen as Wanda Maximoff, and that it would be&nbsp;
directly influenced by the events of WandaVision.

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:34.160
The Marvel faithful were suitably psyched —&nbsp;
but then disaster struck. In January 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:37.840
it was announced that the movie's director,&nbsp;
Scott Derrickson, had left the picture due&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:42.480
to creative differences with Marvel Studios.&nbsp;
Fortunately, fans didn't have to despair for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.480 --> 00:15:47.200
long — because Marvel promptly reached into&nbsp;
its hat and pulled out one heck of a rabbit.

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:51.680
Taking over the picture will be none other&nbsp;
than Sam Raimi, who not only gave us one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:56.880
of the greatest horror-comedies of all time, but&nbsp;
also helped set the entire template for the modern&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.880 --> 00:16:02.880
superhero genre with his Spider-Man trilogy. The&nbsp;
second film of that trilogy, 2004's Spider-Man 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:07.200
is to this day widely considered to be&nbsp;
among the very best comic book movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:11.520
ever made — and for the sheer insanity&nbsp;
promised by the Strange sequel's title,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:16.000
the director seems like an absolutely&nbsp;
perfect fit for the role. Doctor Strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:19.840
in the Multiverse of Madness&nbsp;
releases on March 25th, 2022.

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:23.680
After the tremendous success&nbsp;
of 2018's Black Panther,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:28.560
a sequel seemed like a foregone conclusion.&nbsp;
And sure enough, in the fall of 2018,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:28.560 --> 00:16:32.720
The Hollywood Reporter reported that&nbsp;
Black Panther 2 was officially happening,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:37.120
with original writer-director Ryan Coogler&nbsp;
returning to write and direct the sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:41.600
and celebrated star Chadwick Boseman expected&nbsp;
to reprise his role as King T'Challa.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:47.520
Tragically, however, in August 2020, Boseman&nbsp;
passed away following a four-year struggle with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:52.800
cancer. The news came as a shock to Boseman's&nbsp;
fans and colleagues alike, as the actor had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:58.240
kept his condition and treatment quiet, even as he&nbsp;
continued to work. Following the news of Boseman's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:02.800
passing, Marvel declined to speculate on the&nbsp;
future of the Black Panther franchise, choosing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:07.760
instead to grieve the heartbreaking and shocking&nbsp;
loss of one of the world's brightest stars.

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:13.440
While it's safe to assume Black Panther 2 is still&nbsp;
happening, there's no knowing right now when that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:18.800
will be, or what form the story will take. While&nbsp;
some have speculated that his on-screen sister&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:24.000
Shuri may take up the Black Panther mantle, as she&nbsp;
does in the comics, the pain of Boseman's passing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:28.560
is still too fresh for anyone to publicly&nbsp;
commit to a direction for the franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:32.960
One thing that is certain, however, is that&nbsp;
whenever Black Panther 2 does make its way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:37.920
the screen, both the story and its characters&nbsp;
will find a suitable way to honor their king.

